t a whisky festival in Ayr (and\n                            perhaps enjoyed it slightly more than we should have). After some food and a snooze on the\n                            train back to Glasgow we went for a few pints&mdash;and that’s when the idea came to us!\n                            This concept of allowing people to\n                            <a href=\"create.html\">have their very own bottle of Scotch</a>... through a website!\n                        </p>\n                        <p>\n                            We were so excited! We discussed it more, drew up sketches, concept mocks, the works. Slowly\n                            but surely life got in the way and this idea was put back in the whisky cabinet until such a\n                            time arose that we said to each other \"let’s do it\". And we did. Whisky Blender was\n                            officially established in 2011... and we've been having a dram guid time ever since!\n                        </p>\n                        <span class=\"wb-photo-holder wb-about-photo-acrospire\">\n                            <img class=\"wb-full-width\" src=\"images/about/wb-acrospire.png\" alt=\"Andy & Drew polaroid\"\n                        /></span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>",
